faq:
  - question: "Can I use Grosby Group images on YouTube?"
    answer: "Yes. Images licensed through Grosby Group are cleared for commercial use on YouTube, including monetised channels. The license covers use as thumbnails, in-video imagery, and channel art. You receive a license document confirming the permitted use for each image you download."
  - question: "What types of content are available for creators?"
    answer: "Celebrity and entertainment photography is the core of our creator offering: red carpet, concerts, candid, and exclusive portraits. We also carry sports, fashion, lifestyle, travel, and food content. All images are sourced from the world's leading agencies including Mega, Splash, Instar, Backgrid, and AFP."
  - question: "Which platforms are covered by the license?"
    answer: "A standard creator license covers Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Facebook, X (Twitter), Pinterest, and your own website or blog. If you need coverage for additional platforms or territories, contact our team, as extended licenses are available."
  - question: "How is creator pricing structured?"
    answer: "Creator accounts are priced differently from our publisher accounts, with licensing fees structured for individual and small-team use. Pricing depends on image usage, platform, and audience size. Contact our team or open an account to see the full creator pricing schedule."
  - question: "How quickly can I access and publish content after opening an account?"
    answer: "Most creator accounts are reviewed and activated within one business day. Once active, you can search, download, and publish immediately. There is no minimum order and no waiting period between licensing and publication."
